   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the financial services law, in relation to litigation funding;\nto amend a chapter of the laws of 2025 amending the general business law\nrelating to consumer litigation funding, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 1104-A and A. 804-C, relating to the legislative intent and the\neffectiveness thereof; and to repeal article 39-H of the general business law\nrelating to customer litigation funding",
    "basePrintNo": "S8808",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8808-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2 & 4, Chap of 2025; rpld Art 39-H, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.1104-A & A.804-C); add Art 10 §§1001 - 1011, Fin Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Financial Services Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8808\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the financial services law, in relation to litigation\nfunding; to amend a chapter of the laws of 2025 amending the general\nbusiness law relating to consumer litigation funding, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 1104-A and A. 804-C, relating to the legis-\nlative intent and the effectiveness thereof; and to repeal article 39-H\nof the general business law relating to customer litigation funding\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2025, c.645, to amend the scope of\napplicable contracts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter amendment by making\nseveral technical amendments for clarity, redefining \"charges\" to refer\nto anything paid pursuant to a litigation funding contract, adds\nlanguage to clarify the contact has to tell the consumer how and when\nthe consumer is obligated to pay plus a statement that the money may\nconstitute taxable income.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 645 of the Laws of 2025. 5.1104-A and\nA.804-C, both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June\n2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the financial services law, in\nrelation to litigation funding, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.1104-A and A.804-C, takes effect.\n",
